---
Determine the repository default branch. If the current branch is that default branch, leave `{{workflow.file}}` unchanged and stop.
{{#workflow.issue}}
{{h2}}Verify Completion
{{#project_flags.openspec}}
- If the issue corresponds with an OpenSpec change:
  1. Check that all OpenSpec tasks are marked complete using `openspec list`
  2. Verify the OpenSpec issue shows as complete
  3. Reference {{#resource}}context/openspec{{/resource}} for OpenSpec details if needed
{{/project_flags.openspec}}
- Ensure that the implementation plan is up to date.
  1. Verify all tasks in the implementation plan `{{workflow.plan}}` are marked complete
  2. If tasks cannot be confirmed as complete, inform the user and STOP
{{/workflow.issue}}
Before stashing, perform every completion check in the reset instructions. If any check requires you to stop, do not stash or change `{{workflow.file}}`.
If the worktree has uncommitted changes, ask the user whether to stash them. If they accept, stash every change including untracked files with `git stash push --include-untracked`; apply the reset steps; then always restore the stash with `git stash pop`. If restoration conflicts, stop and report the conflict.
If the user declines the stash, stop without changing `{{workflow.file}}`.
Apply the reset steps only when the current branch is not the default branch, completion checks passed, and the worktree is clean or the user accepted the stash.
{{>workflow-reset-body}}
